# act (https://github.com/nektos/act) configuration for this repository.
# act appends the arguments from ~/.actrc, ~/.config/act/actrc, and this
# ./.actrc; keeping these here scopes them to this repo rather than the machine.

# Map GitHub's ubuntu-latest to catthehacker's "medium" image, which includes
# sudo, apt, git, and node -- the tooling release.yml's run steps assume. act's
# tiny default image (node:slim) lacks sudo/apt and cannot run them.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# No --container-architecture pin: act runs the container natively on the host
# architecture, and release.yml selects its downloads from `uname -m`, so an
# arm64 host is served by arm64 assets. Pinning linux/amd64 on an Apple Silicon
# host puts every step behind the Podman VM's qemu emulation, where the
# Bun-compiled Claude Code installer that install-and-verify.sh fetches dies with
# SIGSEGV. Native execution avoids that and is faster. Add the pin back only to
# reproduce an amd64-specific CI result, and expect the install step to crash.
